  "passage": "Archaeologists found an ancient trash pit. It contained broken pottery, fish bones, seeds, and burned wood.\nStudents thought trash sounded unimportant. The guide explained that trash can reveal what people ate, made, traded, and threw away.\nThe class then studied their own school trash for one day, wearing gloves and recording categories. They found food waste, plastic wrappers, paper, and many unfinished drinks.\nThey realized future historians could learn about them from what they wasted.\nTrash is embarrassing because it shows habits without politeness. That is why it can be honest evidence. What people throw away tells a story.",
